Main Menu specification

Goal
- Add a dedicated MENU mode without overloading the existing LIVE / EDIT screens.
- Keep operation two-handed and visible: ENC1 = navigation / enter, ENC3 = value / back, ENC2 SW = dedicated home / confirm action where needed.
- Avoid a popup. MENU mode should rewrite the whole content area under the header.

Display concept
- MENU mode removes BPM and transport from the header area.
- Header uses a yellow badge with black text, same visual language as EDIT.
- Background stays black unless a later page proves it needs a panel treatment.
- Footer gets menu-specific labels.
- Standard menu pages use a simple scrollable list.
- Dense message editor pages get their own layout and do not try to stay inside the generic list page.

Header badges
- MENU
- BANKS
- BANK 1 .. BANK 8
- BANK EDIT
- FUNCTION BTN
- ACTIVE MSG
- INACTIVE MSG
- DEVICES
- DEVICE 1 .. DEVICE 8
- GLOBAL
- CONFIRM

Footer behavior
- Default menu footer:
	left  = NAV / ENTER
	center = HOME
	right = VALUE / BACK
- Confirmation footer:
	left  = blank
	center = YES
	right = NO

Control model
- ENC2 SW steps to the next bank from LIVE.
- ENC2 turn cycles through presets within the current bank in LIVE.
- ENC1 turn moves the cursor within the current list or page.
- ENC1 press enters the selected submenu or starts editing the selected field.
- ENC3 turn changes tempo in LIVE and changes the selected value when the current row is a leaf field.
- ENC3 SW enters MENU from LIVE, then backs out one level inside MENU.
- ENC2 SW acts as HOME inside MENU pages.
- ENC2 SW acts as YES on confirmation screens.

Working assumption for HOME
- HOME returns to the top-level Main Menu, not directly back to LIVE.
- Exiting MENU entirely can still be done by backing out from Main Menu.

Main Menu tree
- Banks
- Devices
- Global

Banks branch
- BANKS page is a scroll list:
	- Bank 1
	- Bank 2
	- Bank 3
	- Bank 4
	- Bank 5
	- Bank 6
	- Bank 7
	- Bank 8
- Selecting a bank opens that bank's edit space.
- Working assumption: selecting a bank in MENU chooses the target bank for editing only and does not force LIVE mode to switch to that bank immediately.

Bank Edit page
- Bank Name
- Wet / Dry
- Function Button

Bank Edit fields
- Bank Name
	- Smaller-font text editing.
	- Limit: 12 characters.
- Wet / Dry
	- Toggle: Yes / No.
	- If enabled, LIVE mode shows a small W/D badge after the bank name.
	- Badge style: charcoal background, black text.
- Function Button
	- Opens its own submenu.

Function Button submenu
- Name
- Active Label
- Inactive Label
- Active Messages
- Inactive Messages

Function Button fields
- Name
	- Smaller-font text editing.
	- Limit: 6 characters.
	- Current default example: Vita.
- Active Label
	- Smaller-font text editing.
	- Limit: 6 characters.
	- Current default example: undead.
- Inactive Label
	- Smaller-font text editing.
	- Limit: 6 characters.
	- Current default example: dead.

Function Button message pages
- Active Messages and Inactive Messages each get a dedicated dense page.
- Each page contains 8 rows total.
- Rows 1-4: arbitrary Program Change messages
	- Format: CH: --  PRG: ---
- Rows 5-8: arbitrary CC messages
	- Format: CH: --  CC: ---  VAL: ---
- These messages are not tied to configured devices.
- Any MIDI channel is valid as long as it is a Program Change or CC message.
- Keep explicit unused sentinel behavior so rows can be blank.

Devices branch
- DEVICES page is a scroll list:
	- Device 1
	- Device 2
	- Device 3
	- Device 4
	- Device 5
	- Device 6
	- Device 7
	- Device 8
- Empty devices still stay visible.

Device Edit page
- Name
- Max Preset Number
- Channel
- Active CC
- Bypass CC
- Level CC
- Tap-SW CC
- Init Device

Device Edit fields
- Name
	- Smaller-font text editing.
	- Limit: 4 characters.
	- Intended to replace CH n prefixes in LIVE mode when non-empty.
	- Example display target: ECHO: or VERB: instead of CH 1:.
- Max Preset Number
	- Range: 1-127.
- Channel
	- Range: 1-16.
	- If Name is empty, LIVE mode falls back to CH n: formatting.
	- Channel must update the actual runtime device definition.
- Active CC
	- Format: CC: ---  VAL: ---
- Bypass CC
	- Format: CC: ---  VAL: ---
- Level CC
	- Format: CC: ---  VAL: ---
- Tap-SW CC
	- Format: CC: ---  VAL: ---
- Init Device
	- Resets the device config to unused defaults.
	- Requires confirmation.

Init Device confirmation page
- Header badge: CONFIRM
- Body text example: INIT DEVICE 3?
- ENC2 SW = YES
- ENC3 SW = NO
- This avoids accidental confirmation from normal back-button mashing.

Global branch
- Startup Delay
- Sync Style
- Brightness

Global fields
- Startup Delay
	- Range: 0-60 sec.
	- Purpose: wait for slower pedals to boot before normal behavior is expected.
- Sync Style
	- Options:
		- MIDI clock
		- Tap Tempo CC
	- MIDI clock:
		- Tap switch calculates tempo.
		- Firmware sends MIDI clock to pedals.
	- Tap Tempo CC:
		- Firmware does not send MIDI clock.
		- Firmware sends each device's configured Tap-SW CC instead.
		- Intended as fallback for pedals that react badly to MIDI clock jitter.
- Brightness
	- Range: 0-255.

Apply / save model
- Global settings apply immediately.
- Device edits save on leaving the device submenu.
- Bank edits save on leaving the bank submenu.
- Function Button edits save on leaving that submenu.
- Dense message pages save on leaving that page or its parent submenu.

Implementation constraints and notes
- This work changes data ownership in multiple places:
	- fixed bank names -> editable bank config
	- fixed device definitions -> editable runtime device config
	- fixed function-button labels/messages -> editable config
	- fixed global constants -> editable runtime settings
- The safe path is incremental, not one large merge.

Staged rollout plan
- Phase 1: configuration model only
	- Add runtime config structs for banks, devices, function button, and globals.
	- Seed them from current fixed defaults.
- Phase 2: live lookups
	- Route LIVE rendering and runtime behavior through config accessors.
	- Preserve current visible behavior.
- Phase 3: persistence
	- Persist the new config data with versioned flash storage.
	- Verify migration from defaults works cleanly.
- Phase 4: menu shell
	- Add MENU mode, header badge, footer labels, list-page drawing, and navigation only.
- Phase 5: simple editors
	- Bank name, Wet / Dry, device name, channel, max preset, globals.
- Phase 6: dense editors and confirmations
	- Function Button Active / Inactive Messages.
	- Init Device confirmation flow.

Open items to revisit during implementation
